libpmhost host patch: what the HOST build changes in the firmware, and nothing
the iron runs (every hunk is behind PMHOST, which only tools/picomem/shim sets).

  picomem.cpp        the PIO bus loop becomes shim/include/pmhost_isa.h, and
                     main() is pmh_fw_main, run on the card thread
  dev_audiomix.cpp   pico_pic.h on the host too (the PIC is compiled here)
  pm_pccmd.cpp       pccmd_wait() yields: the PC is the emulator
  dev_picomem_io.cpp the port-4 transfer loop yields likewise
  pm_cmd.cpp         the mouse report the USB host path sends, sent off
                     pm_mouse() instead (no tinyusb on the host)

Cut against the pin plus patches/fw/ (tools/martypc/README.md's rule).
GPL-2.0-or-later, like the firmware.

